# PocketCHIP variant: LXDE desktop with a touch-sized bottom panel.

# Desktop: LXDE (Openbox + lxpanel). The panel is configured for the 480x272
# touchscreen; i3 stays installed as a fallback session.
lxappearance
lxde-common
lxinput
lxmenu-data
lxpanel
lxrandr
lxsession
lxsession-edit
openbox

# Desktop runtime and PICO-8/SunVox dependencies.
python3-gi
unclutter
upower
libsdl2-2.0-0
libsdl2-image-2.0-0
libgl1
libegl1
libgles2

# Applications used from the LXDE panel and menu.
pcmanfm
mousepad

# The security and OSINT toolkits are not part of the default image: they made
# the NAND rootfs unnecessarily large on a device that also carries PICO-8 and
# SunVox. `pocketchip-toolkits` installs them on demand, in groups, from the
# LXDE menu (see docs/variants.md). Everyday network diagnostics such as nmap,
# tcpdump, iw and wireless-tools stay in the base package list.
